{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing task #5426 in a cobbler generation pipeline: \"[stitch] cmd/factor: srd065 R2.1-R2.4\". The task requires extending the existing cmd/factor implementation (which already has R1.1-R1.4) with R2.1-R2.4 functionality (stdin mode and input handling), and adding differential tests for these new requirements. The specific requirements are:\n   - R2.1: Read integers from stdin when no arguments given\n   - R2.2: Accept integers up to 2^63-1 (int64 max)\n   - R2.3: Skip blank lines in stdin mode without output or error\n   - R2.4: Print error to stderr for non-integer/negative input, continue processing remaining inputs\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (gfactor)\n   - DiffTest struct with Stdin field for piping input, ExitCode for asserting non-zero exits\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests and testutils.BuildBinary for test harness\n   - exec.LookPath(\"gfactor\") with t.Skip for graceful degradation\n   - SIGPIPE handler via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - strconv.ParseInt for int64 parsing\n   - Trial division factorization algorithm\n   - LC_ALL=C for deterministic output comparison\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd065-factor.yaml**\n     - Full SRD defining all requirements R1-R4 with acceptance criteria\n     - R2 section defines stdin mode and input handling requirements\n     - Non-goals: no arbitrary-precision beyond int64, no advanced algorithms\n   \n   - **cmd/factor/main.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Already has processStdin() (lines 60-74) handling R2.1 and R2.3\n     - Already uses strconv.ParseInt with int64 (line 77) for R2.2\n     - Already handles errors to stderr and continues (lines 53-54, 69-70) for R2.4\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // factor prints the prime factorization of each integer.\n     //\n     // Specification: srd065-factor R1.1-R1.4\n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"bufio\"\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"math\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"strconv\"\n         \"strings\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     \n     const helpText = `Usage: factor [NUMBER]...\n     Print the prime factors of each specified integer.\n     `\n     const versionText = `factor (go-unix-utils) 0.1.0`\n     \n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n             switch os.Args[1] {\n             case \"--help\":\n                 fmt.Print(helpText)\n                 return\n             case \"--version\":\n                 fmt.Println(versionText)\n                 return\n             }\n         }\n         exitCode := 0\n         if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n             exitCode = processArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         } else {\n             exitCode = processStdin()\n         }\n         os.Exit(exitCode)\n     }\n     \n     func processArgs(args []string) int {\n         exitCode := 0\n         for _, arg := range args {\n             if err := factorize(arg); err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"factor: %s\\n\", err)\n                 exitCode = 1\n             }\n         }\n         return exitCode\n     }\n     \n     func processStdin() int {\n         exitCode := 0\n         scanner := bufio.NewScanner(os.Stdin)\n         for scanner.Scan() {\n             line := strings.TrimSpace(scanner.Text())\n             if line == \"\" {\n                 continue\n             }\n             if err := factorize(line); err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"factor: %s\\n\", err)\n                 exitCode = 1\n             }\n         }\n         return exitCode\n     }\n     \n     func factorize(input string) error {\n         n, err := strconv.ParseInt(input, 10, 64)\n         if err != nil {\n             return fmt.Errorf(\"'%s' is not a valid positive integer\", input)\n         }\n         if n < 0 {\n             return fmt.Errorf(\"'%s' is not a valid positive integer\", input)\n         }\n         factors := primeFactors(n)\n         printFactors(n, factors)\n         return nil\n     }\n     \n     func primeFactors(n int64) []int64 {\n         if n <= 1 {\n             return nil\n         }\n         var factors []int64\n         for n%2 == 0 {\n             factors = append(factors, 2)\n             n /= 2\n         }\n         limit := int64(math.Sqrt(float64(n)))\n         for d := int64(3); d <= limit; d += 2 {\n             for n%d == 0 {\n                 factors = append(factors, d)\n                 n /= d\n             }\n             limit = int64(math.Sqrt(float64(n)))\n         }\n         if n > 1 {\n             factors = append(factors, n)\n         }\n         return factors\n     }\n     \n     func printFactors(n int64, factors []int64) {\n         var b strings.Builder\n         fmt.Fprintf(&b, \"%d:\", n)\n         for _, f := range factors {\n             fmt.Fprintf(&b, \" %d\", f)\n         }\n         fmt.Println(b.String())\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/factor/factor_test.go** (existing, needs modification)\n     - Only has argument-mode tests, NO stdin tests, NO error tests\n     - Needs R2.1-R2.4 differential tests added\n     - Full existing code:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package main\n     \n     import (\n         \"os/exec\"\n         \"testing\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n     )\n     \n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n         goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n         refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gfactor\")\n         if err != nil {\n             t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\")\n         }\n         tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n             {Name: \"single_composite\", Args: []string{\"12\"}},\n             {Name: \"number_one\", Args: []string{\"1\"}},\n             {Name: \"prime_number\", Args: []string{\"97\"}},\n             {Name: \"multiple_arguments\", Args: []string{\"6\", \"7\", \"12\", \"1\", \"97\"}},\n             {Name: \"large_composite\", Args: []string{\"1000000\"}},\n             {Name: \"power_of_two\", Args: []string{\"1024\"}},\n             {Name: \"prime_squared\", Args: []string{\"49\"}},\n             {Name: \"two\", Args: []string{\"2\"}},\n             {Name: \"zero\", Args: []string{\"0\"}},\n         }\n         testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - work was interrupted before any modifications were made.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Analyzed existing code and found R2.1-R2.4 functionality appears to already be implemented in main.go\n   - Key issue: The error message format may differ from gfactor's error format. GNU factor uses format like `factor: 'abc' is not a valid positive integer` - need to verify the existing error format matches\n   - The package doc comment only references R1.1-R1.4 and needs to be updated to include R2.1-R2.4\n   - Test file needs new DiffTest entries using the Stdin field for stdin mode, and ExitCode field for error cases\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely long task description with full project context, SRDs, architecture docs, execution constitution, and task details for implementing srd065 R2.1-R2.4 for cmd/factor\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Update cmd/